{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Owe no [F/A]one anyt[Gm7]hing, except to love one [Eb]an[Bb]other
Whoever [F/A]loves the other [Gm7]has fulfilled the [Eb]law
The [Bb]commandments are summed up [F/A]in this simple word
[Gm7]Love your neighbor as yourself, [Eb]that is the road
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The [Bb]hour has already come for [F/A]you to wake from sleep
Sal[Gm7]vation is nearer to us [Eb]now than when we first believed
[Bb]The night is nearly over, [F/A]the day is at hand
Let [Gm7]us cast off the works of dark[Eb]ness, put on the armor [Bb]of [F/A]light [Gm7][Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Live decently, as [F/A]in the daytime, [Gm7]not in carousing
[Eb]Not in drunkenness, [Bb]not in sexual [F/A]immorali[Gm7]ty
Not in quarreling, not in [Eb]jealousy or strife
[Bb]Give no thought to gratifying the [F/A]desires of the flesh
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The [Bb]hour has already come for [F/A]you to wake from sleep
Sal[Gm7]vation is nearer to us now [Eb]than when we first believed
The [Bb]night is nearly over, the [F/A]day is at hand
Let us [Gm7]cast off the works of darkness, [Eb]put on the armor of [Bb]light
